# Cursor Rules for WOTP

# Branch model: a single trunk. See AGENTS.md for the authoritative policy.
# `main` is the canonical project and may be deployed, so confirm with the
# owner before pushing. Work happens on short-lived feature branches that merge
# back into `main`. The old `main` / `feat/self-host` split is retired.

1. Always check the active git branch before editing or committing (`git branch --show-current`).
2. Never commit secrets, tokens, or `.env` files. Every `.env` is untracked; the examples hold placeholders only.
3. Never run a real send. Tests use mock delivery and must not contact Meta, Telegram, or any external service.
4. Ensure all backend tests (`backend/.venv/bin/pytest -q`) and frontend checks (`bun run typecheck`, `bun run lint`, `bun run format:check`) pass before committing.
5. Refer to `AGENTS.md` for the complete policy, dev commands and safety checklist.
